(A) Lemma 5.1 by exact enumeration
  (pq) E sqrt(Lambda_n) - (1-gamma)^n over 20 random (mu, nu, nu_pi), n <= 6: max |difference| = 4.29e-14
  (fd) E sqrt(Lambda) - prod_x (1 - Hel_x) over 50 random kernels on 8 inputs: max |difference| = 5.55e-16
  (wor) E prod a(x_i) without replacement / (mean a)^n over 3386 (population, n) cases: max = 1.000000 (<= 1 required)
  frozen, n=  1: E sqrt(Lambda_n) = 0.970711  vs  (1-gamma)^n = 9.707e-01  (equal: no repeat possible yet)
  frozen, n=  5: E sqrt(Lambda_n) = 0.880057  vs  (1-gamma)^n = 8.619e-01  (the (pq)/(wor) bound fails)
  frozen, n= 20: E sqrt(Lambda_n) = 0.742716  vs  (1-gamma)^n = 5.518e-01  (the (pq)/(wor) bound fails)
  frozen, n=100: E sqrt(Lambda_n) = 0.707115  vs  (1-gamma)^n = 5.117e-02  (the (pq)/(wor) bound fails)
========================================================================================================
(B) Lemma 5.2 (fd form) and Lemma 5.3 (fixed n), exact over all 2^10 label vectors of a fixed domain
  300 random classes (5-39 programs; random, perturbed, deterministic, D-equivalent, sub-probability)
  max over classes and t in [0.5, 1.0, 2.0, 3.0] of P[S_D <= -t] / 2^-t = 0.2006  (Lemma 5.2, fd form; <= 1 required)
  max over classes and t of P[T <= -t] / 2^-t = 0.2253  (Lemma 5.3 at fixed n; <= 1 required)
